o the  ground to quickly grab weapons shields  and harvest materials depending on where  you land you may find yourself in a  fight immediately or you may have a  quiet landing zone that gives you the  opportunity to loot in peace now what's  that about harvesting materials you see  what separates fortnight from other  games in the battle where Al Jean rrah  is the building component you'll have  the option to set up a base and build a  four of  or quickly build a wall and ramp in  front of you if attacked by an enemy in  order to compete with the best you'll  need to master the game's building  component I'm out right now you'll  always have your trusty pickaxe which is  used for harvesting materials that allow  you to build walls ramps floors and  roots you can use the pickaxe to attack  as well but I'd only recommend that if  you have no other option other than that  you have five slots to hold weapons and  healing items such as shields bandages  or med kits it's up to you to decide  what you want to carry fortnight  supports a variety of play styles which  means you can rush people with shotguns  or play stealth and engage from long  range with a sniper rifle I got one  there's one chasing me in solos enemies  go down immediately after you deplete  their health which can be up to 200 hit  points consisting of their base health  which is 100 points and shield which  also goes up to 100 points for a total  of 200 in duo's or squads players with  teammates still alive will become  knocked when their health is drained you  can choose to fully eliminate them from  there or find their teammate to finish  them both off if the teammate gets the  better of you however they'll then be  able to revive their fallen teammate if  they dispatch you quickly enough you see  when teammates enter the nacht state  they'll have 100 health that starts  ticking down immediately they can only  crawl on the ground and can't shoot or  run away shortly after a match begins a  white circle will appear on your map  which is the zone everyone must start  moving toward with the appearance of the  circle a storm will slowly begin moving  in making its way closer and closer to  that inner white circle a timer will be  displayed on screen letting you know  exactly how much time you have left  before the storm will reach you if you  get caught in the storm  you'll take continuous damage until you  exit or die the circle will continue  getting smaller and smaller and if need  be the circle will disappear entirely  for the final zone the shrinking of the  playable area will force everyone to  engage eventually you can only hide for  so long once you die or hopefully win  your match  everything resets and you're taken back  to the main screen and trust me you'll  want to load up for another match again  again and again you do earn points by  completing various challenges that reset  periodically some daily and some weekly  these points can earn you various skins  emotes and other cosmetic items you  don't have to spend a penny on fortnight  Battle Royale  but if you enjoy the cosmetics and trust  me you probably will you'll get the most  bang for your buck by purchasing the  Battle Pass which costs nine hundred and  fifty bucks which is the equivalent of  nine dollars and fifty cents considering  mini skins in the game cost between  fifteen and twenty dollars alone the  battle pass is a great value if you like  the cosmetics it contains and plan on  playing a lot you see buying the battle  pass alone won't unlock every skin  inside you'll need to actually play the  game in order to rank up your battle  pass during each fortnight season which  lasts about ten weeks and there you have  it folks now you know all about the  basics a fortnight Battle Royale in  upcoming videos we're gonna tackle even  more to help you better understand the  weapons at your disposal how to build  and more if you enjoyed this video and  that sounds like something of interest  to you 